{
  "id": "expressions-owed-axes",
  "description": "M3b owed-case catalog for ExpressionEvaluator. One key per expression SHAPE, deliberately generic ('value', 'left', 'right', 'count') so a single compiled expression can be driven with every runtime operand type from the case file. Covers the four axes no corpus expression ever mentioned (definiteness, classifier, clusivity, animacy), '!=' on every language-form axis, '<=' (which appeared in no expression at all), constant-on-the-left equality, and the constant-pair forms that are the only things able to execute canBeEqualExpressionValue's same-type and NUMBER/CARDINALITY-NUMBER/ORDINALITY rules. 'ja' carries only the constant-pair numeric keys, so the LOCALE-driven classification of a numeric LITERAL is pinned against 'en' (1 is 'one' in en and 'other' in ja).",
